# Blog topics come from a Google gap

Before a new title, compare the live posts and the unused slate rows with Google result pages for the same job.

Write the next article only when both are true:

1. Google already shows results for that search.
2. This site has no page that answers it.

Record the search on the slate row before drafting. A checklist line with no result page stays unused. These have no result page: “sin palabras de informática”, “que no pida el móvil”, “de dónde salió cada dato”.

Do not invent a search volume. Do not put a ranking, a position, or a traffic number in the article.

Open gaps from the last comparison: a price that was right and is now stale on a live post; whether Google treats an AI blog as spam (“abuso de contenido a gran escala”); “cómo titular un artículo de blog”.
